(Discrepancy 2 - minimal repro, RESOLVED by vox #281. The vox 0.4.15 manual
 had two bullets: text to number "fails if text is not a valid number and
 sets the error flag", and a non-default-base cast "stops parsing at the
 first character invalid for that base" and "does not set the error
 flag". The 0.4.15 compiler did neither: it stopped at the first invalid
 character in every base and set the flag only when nothing parsed, so
 this probe printed 12, then the base 10 total failure and 0, then 18,
 then the hex total failure and 0.
 The manual now has one rule for every base (LANGUAGE.md:2158-2165,
 2223-2230): a text is a number only when the whole text is one, and a
 text known only at run time that is not a number raises the error flag
 and leaves a declaration holding 0 (LANGUAGE.md:2243-2248). All four
 casts below now fail. Re-recorded 2026-10-13 on vox main a0a2ecc.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D2.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   base 10 partial: flag SET
   0
   base 10 total failure: flag SET
   0
   hex partial: flag SET
   0
   hex total failure: flag SET
   0
)
a text called partial is "12xy".
a number called 'base ten partial' is partial as a number.
On error Print "base 10 partial: flag SET".
Print 'base ten partial'.
a text called rubbish is "abc".
a number called 'base ten total' is rubbish as a number.
On error Print "base 10 total failure: flag SET".
Print 'base ten total'.
a text called mixed is "12g5".
a number called 'hex partial' is mixed as a hex number.
On error Print "hex partial: flag SET".
Print 'hex partial'.
a text called letters is "zzz".
a number called 'hex total' is letters as a hex number.
On error Print "hex total failure: flag SET".
Print 'hex total'.
